🔹 CATEGORY 1 — Conditional Logic Across Many Rules
Example:

“Classify transactions into risk levels”

Rules like:

Amount > 500 → High Risk

Crypto & Amount > 200 → Medium Risk

Else → Low Risk

Python (clean & scalable):
def risk_level(row):
    if row["Amount"] > 500:
        return "High"
    elif row["Category"] == "Crypto" and row["Amount"] > 200:
        return "Medium"
    else:
        return "Low"

df["Risk_Level"] = df.apply(risk_level, axis=1)


🔹 Hard in Excel
🔹 Ugly in SQL
🔹 Clean in Python



